```
id: SPL-015
name: Process access to LSASS with dump-capable rights
description: Sysmon process access events against LSASS from untrusted source images.
platform: Splunk
mitre_tactic: Credential Access
mitre_technique: T1003.001 OS Credential Dumping: LSASS Memory
severity: High
data_source: index=sysmon (process access)
false_positives: Security agents and diagnostic tools.
tuning: Maintain an allow lookup of signed security agents by source image path.
test_method: Run an Atomic Red Team LSASS test on an isolated lab endpoint.
owner: <OWNER>
status: Draft
last_review: 2026-11-19
```
index=sysmon sourcetype="XmlWinEventLog:Microsoft-Windows-Sysmon/Operational" EventCode=10 TargetImage="*\\lsass.exe" earliest=-1h
    GrantedAccess IN ("0x1010","0x1410","0x1438","0x143a","0x1fffff")
| search NOT [| inputlookup lsass_allowed_sources.csv | fields SourceImage]
| table _time host SourceImage GrantedAccess CallTrace
| sort - _time
